55,"question":{"id":81862,"exampleId":4124,"difficulty":1}},{"id":62288215,"studentId":57975,"choices":null,"selectedChoice":1,"selectId":0,"correct":1,"timeElapsed":15743,"question":{"id":166551,"exampleId":4124,"difficulty":2}}],"completedStr":"Completed on Thu, Oct 15th","exampleAnswers":[{"id":4134,"number":1,"title":"The Domain of a Transformed Logarithmic Function","answers":[{"id":62288006,"created":"2026-10-15T17:09:30.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13200,"number":1,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 5:09 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":41247,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":4134,"text":"<p>Determine the domain of the function $f(x) = -\\dfrac{1}{4} \\log_7(2x - 3) + 2.$</p>\n","choice1":"$x \\in \\left( \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\infty \\right)$","choice2":"$x \\in \\left( -\\infty, \\infty \\right)$","choice3":"$x \\in \\left( -3, \\infty \\right)$","choice4":"$x \\in \\left( -\\dfrac{3}{2}, \\dfrac{3}{2} \\right)$","choice5":"$x \\in \\left( 3, \\infty \\right)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>The domain of $y = \\log_{7}{x}$ is\n\\[\nx \\gt 0.\n\\]</p>\n<p>To find the domain of $f(x),$ we replace $x$ with $2x - 3$ in the above inequality. This gives\n\\[\n2x - 3 &gt; 0.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Solving this inequality, we get\n\\begin{align}\n2x-3 &&gt; 0\\\\[5pt]\n2x &&gt; 3\\\\[5pt]\nx &&gt; \\dfrac 3 2\n\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Therefore, the domain of $y = f(x)$ is $x \\in \\left( \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\infty \\right).$</p>\n","topic":{"id":1610,"name":"Properties of Transformed Logarithmic Functions"},"example":{"id":4134,"title":"The Domain of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"},"group":{"id":86069,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14247089,"answer":{"id":62288006,"cread":"2026-10-15T17:09:30.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13200},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62288024,"created":"2026-10-15T17:09:44.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":10188,"number":2,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 5:09 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:10","question":{"id":4115,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":4134,"text":"<p>Find the domain of the function $f(x) =  \\log{\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}-1\\right)} - 4.$</p>\n","choice1":"$x\\in\\left(2, \\infty\\right)$","choice2":"$x\\in\\left(\\dfrac 1 2, \\infty\\right)$","choice3":"$x\\in\\left(-2, \\infty\\right)$","choice4":"$x\\in\\left[\\dfrac 1 2, \\infty\\right)$","choice5":"$x\\in\\left[2, \\infty\\right)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>The domain of $y = \\log{x}$ is\n\\[\nx \\gt 0.\n\\]</p>\n<p>To find the domain of $f(x),$ we replace $x$ with $\\dfrac{x}{2}-1$ in the above inequality. This gives\n\\[\n\\dfrac{x}{2}-1 &gt; 0.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Solving this inequality, we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{x}{2}-1 &&gt; 0 \\\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{x}{2} &&gt; 1 \\\\[5pt]\n\t\tx &&gt;2.\n\t}\n\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore, the domain of $y = f(x)$ is $x \\in \\left(2, \\infty\\right).$</p>\n","topic":{"id":1610,"name":"Properties of Transformed Logarithmic Functions"},"example":{"id":4134,"title":"The Domain of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"},"group":{"id":86068,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14247089,"answer":{"id":62288024,"cread":"2026-10-15T17:09:44.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":10188},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":4137,"number":2,"title":"The Vertical Asymptote of a Transformed Logarithmic Function","answers":[{"id":62288099,"created":"2026-10-15T17:10:04.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13844,"number":3,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 5:10 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":81990,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":4137,"text":"<p>Find the equation of the vertical asymptote of the function $f(x) = \\log(2x)-8.$</p>\n","choice1":"$x=0$","choice2":"$x=\\dfrac 12$","choice3":"$x=2$","choice4":"$x=\\dfrac{1}{4}$","choice5":"$x=8$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>The equation of the vertical asymptote of the function $y = \\log{x}$ is $x=0.$</p>\n<p>To find the equation of the vertical asymptote of $f(x)$, we set the argument of the logarithmic term equal to zero, and solve for $x.$ This gives\n\\begin{align}\n2x & = 0\\\\[3pt]\nx & = 0.\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Therefore, the equation of the vertical asymptote is $x = 0.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":1610,"name":"Properties of Transformed Logarithmic Functions"},"example":{"id":4137,"title":"The Vertical Asymptote of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"},"group":{"id":86073,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14247089,"answer":{"id":62288099,"cread":"2026-10-15T17:10:04.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13844},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62288121,"created":"2026-10-15T17:10:22.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13371,"number":4,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 5:10 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":81991,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":4137,"text":"<p>Find the equation of the vertical asymptote of the function $f(x) = 10\\ln(5x).$</p>\n","choice1":"$x = 0$","choice2":"$x = 10$","choice3":"$x = 5$","choice4":"$x = \\dfrac{1}{10}$","choice5":"$x = \\dfrac 15$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>The equation of the vertical asymptote of the function $y = \\ln{x}$ is $x=0.$</p>\n<p>To find the equation of the vertical asymptote of $f(x)$, we set the argument of the logarithmic term equal to zero, and solve for $x.$ This gives\n\\begin{align}\n5x & = 0\\\\[3pt]\nx & = 0.\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Therefore, the equation of the vertical asymptote is $x = 0.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":1610,"name":"Properties of Transformed Logarithmic Functions"},"example":{"id":4137,"title":"The Vertical Asymptote of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"},"group":{"id":86073,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14247089,"answer":{"id":62288121,"cread":"2026-10-15T17:10:22.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13371},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":4135,"number":3,"title":"The Root of a Transformed Logarithmic Function","answers":[{"id":62288137,"created":"2026-10-15T17:10:41.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11396,"number":5,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 5:10 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:11","question":{"id":81997,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":4135,"text":"<p>Find the root of $f(x) = \\ln(2x+7).$</p>\n","choice1":"$x=-3$ ","choice2":"$x=-\\dfrac 72$  ","choice3":"$x=3$  ","choice4":"$x=4$  ","choice5":"$x=-2$  ","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0\\mathbin{:}$\n\\[\n\\ln(2x+7) = 0\n\\]</p>\n<p>We solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\\ln(2x+7) & = 0\\\\[5pt]\n\ne^{\\ln(2x+7)} & = e^0\\\\[5pt]\n\n2x+7 & = 1\\\\[5pt]\n\n2x & = -6\\\\[5pt]\n\nx & = -3\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Therefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=-3.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":1610,"name":"Properties of Transformed Logarithmic Functions"},"example":{"id":4135,"title":"The Root of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"},"group":{"id":86070,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14247089,"answer":{"id":62288137,"cread":"2026-10-15T17:10:41.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11396},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62288164,"created":"2026-10-15T17:11:00.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15300,"number":6,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 5:11 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":81999,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":4135,"text":"<p>Find the root of $f(x) = 2\\log_2(x)-6.$</p>\n","choice1":"$x=8$ ","choice2":"$x=6$  ","choice3":"$x=4$   ","choice4":"$x=16$    ","choice5":"$x=1$    ","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0\\mathbin{:}$\n\\[\n2\\log_2(x)-6 = 0\n\\]</p>\n<p>We solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n2\\log_2(x)-6 & = 0\\\\[5pt]\n\n2\\log_2(x) & = 6\\\\[5pt]\n\\log_2(x) & = 3\\\\[5pt]\n\n2^{\\log_2(x)} & = 2^3\\\\[5pt]\n\nx & = 8\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Therefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=8.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":1610,"name":"Properties of Transformed Logarithmic Functions"},"example":{"id":4135,"title":"The Root of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"},"group":{"id":86070,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14247089,"answer":{"id":62288164,"cread":"2026-10-15T17:11:00.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15300},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":4124,"number":4,"title":"The Range of a Transformed Logarithmic Function","answers":[{"id":62288188,"created":"2026-10-15T17:11:22.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":10855,"number":7,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 5:11 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:11","question":{"id":81862,"for